repository-code: "https://github.com/radical-cybertools/workflow-mini-apps"
abstract: >-
  The Workflow Mini-App framework provides the environment
  to build compact, self-contained applications that emulate
  key aspects of larger scientific workflows, enabling
  researchers to explore, test, and optimize computational
  tasks without running the full-scale workflow. By
  leveraging RADICAL tools, such as RADICAL-EnTK (for
  workflow orchestration) and RADICAL-Pilot (for dynamic
  resource management), these WF MiniApps can efficiently
  schedule and execute multiple heterogeneous tasks across
  HPC systems, clusters, or cloud infrastructures.
